# Server-side (Next.js)

There is no separate backend service (ADR 0006 supersedes ADR 0003). Do not add
Python, FastAPI, Docker, or database code to `backend/`; it is a placeholder
README only.

- Route Handlers are HTTP only: validation, status codes, composition. Business
  rules live in `domain/` and `application/`.
- Modules that read secrets or call external services import `server-only`.
  Secrets never use `NEXT_PUBLIC_`. `.env.example` holds empty placeholders only.
- Client Components never import `config/`, `infrastructure/`, or provider code.
- No page render or public Route Handler calls a provider per request; follow
  ADR 0009 (cache/snapshot, bounded retries, request budget). No pass-through
  proxy routes.
- Provider (Zoho) DTOs stay in `infrastructure/` behind mappers (ADR 0005).
  Do not invent Zoho endpoints, fields, scopes, or limits.
- No database, ORM, migration tool, or KV store unless ADR 0008 is amended and
  accepted.

Match `docs/architecture/BACKEND_ARCHITECTURE.md` (server-side architecture).
